{
  "_comment": [
    "Example machine-local Claude Code settings.",
    "Copy this file to settings.local.json and edit it, or just let",
    "`bash claude/sync.sh --apply` fill it in from what Claude Code wrote.",
    "This file is a template shared on GitHub; settings.local.json is gitignored.",
    "",
    "Instructions:",
    "  1. cp claude/settings.local.json.example claude/settings.local.json",
    "  2. Remove this _comment key and keep only the settings you need.",
    "  3. bash claude/install.sh",
    "",
    "Semantics: this overlay is applied on top of claude/settings.json at the",
    "TOP-LEVEL KEY level. A key present here replaces the base's key outright",
    "(it is not merged entry by entry), and a key set to null removes it.",
    "Keys absent here fall through to the base unchanged.",
    "",
    "Do NOT put permissions or hooks here. They are shared guardrails and",
    "deny-check.sh treats a missing deny list as a reason to block, not allow.",
    "",
    "Not to be confused with the repository's own .claude/settings.local.json,",
    "which is Claude Code's project-scoped settings file and IS tracked."
  ],

  "theme": "dark",
  "effortLevel": "xhigh",

  "extraKnownMarketplaces": {
    "example-private-marketplace": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "your-org/your-plugins"
      },
      "autoUpdate": true
    }
  },

  "enabledPlugins": {
    "example-plugin@example-private-marketplace": true
  }
}
